    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57705": {
      "title": "Research IT Specialist",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Research IT Specialist Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Research IT Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Division of Research seeks a technology professional with strong technical support, systems administration, and customer service skills to support enterprise research technologies and digital initiatives. The successful candidate will contribute to research operations, technology modernization, website services, AI-enabled tools, and continuous improvement efforts that enhance support services and operational efficiency. Please note that his position may require occasional extended hours for upgrades, events, testing, or operational deadlines outside of normal business hours defined as Monday-Friday 8am-5pm. Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Certifications Project Portfolio or Documentation Samples Veteran's Preference Documents Additional Supporting Materials Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026650 Posting/Functional Title Research IT Specialist University Pay Plan Title Electronic Research Specialist Location San Marcos Department Research IT Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $6,000.00 - $6,483.72 Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Bachelor’s degree and three years of related experience. Experience supporting hardware, operating systems, enterprise applications, endpoint technologies, networking, and user devices in a multi-user environment. Experience troubleshooting software, authentication, access, application performance, and systems integration issues. Experience supporting websites, web applications, content management systems, or web-based platforms. Strong and responsive customer service, communication, training, documentation, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and safeguard sensitive institutional and research information. Preferred Qualifications Experience supporting eRA systems such as Kuali, Cayuse, Huron, InfoEd, Streamlyne, or similar platforms. Experience supporting AI tools, workflow automation solutions, analytics platforms, dashboards, or reporting systems. Experience with website platforms such as WordPress, SharePoint, Drupal, Gato, Calico, or similar technologies. Experience with endpoint management, software deployment, cybersecurity practices, vulnerability remediation, or IT asset management. Familiarity with research administration, sponsored programs, compliance operations, or higher education environments. Job Description The Research IT Specialist provides operational and technical support for the Division of Research technology environment, including desktop systems, enterprise applications, electronic research administration (eRA) platforms, websites, conferencing technologies, and emerging AI-enabled tools. This position serves as a primary resource for troubleshooting hardware, software, authentication, networking, and systems access issues while supporting secure, reliable, and efficient technology operations. The Specialist assists with administration of research administration systems, website maintenance, workflow automation tools, analytics resources, and user support services. The successful candidate is a customer-focused technology professional with strong troubleshooting skills, the ability to manage multiple priorities, and the ability to communicate technical information to diverse audiences. Job Duties Provide technical support for desktop hardware, laptops, mobile devices, printers, operating systems, peripherals, and enterprise applications. Troubleshoot and resolve hardware, software, networking, authentication, access, and systems integration issues. Support administration and user assistance for eRA systems and related proposal, compliance, and award management platforms. Maintain user accounts, permissions, role-based security, and access controls for departmental and enterprise systems. Support departmental websites, web applications, content management systems, and web-based services. Assist with implementation and support of workflow automation, reporting tools, dashboards, AI-enabled solutions, and operational technologies. Support conferencing, audiovisual, livestreaming, and hybrid meeting technologies for research operations and events. Coordinate with university IT, vendors, developers, and functional offices to resolve issues and implement technology improvements. Create and maintain technical documentation, training materials, knowledge-base resources, inventory records, and standard operating procedures. Monitor technology resources for performance, security, reliability, and compliance and perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information to Applicants The Division of Research seeks a technology professional with strong technical support, systems administration, and customer service skills to support enterprise research technologies and digital initiatives. The successful candidate will contribute to research operations, technology modernization, website services, AI-enabled tools, and continuous improvement efforts that enhance support services and operational efficiency. Please note that his position may require occasional extended hours for upgrades, events, testing, or operational deadlines outside of normal business hours defined as Monday-Friday 8am-5pm. Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Certifications Project Portfolio or Documentation Samples Veteran’s Preference Documents Additional Supporting Materials Job Open Date 07/03/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57578 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Portfolio DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Additional Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57514": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Nontenure Faculty Pool - Department of Biology Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Nontenure Faculty Pool - Department of Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Nontenure Faculty Pool - Department of Biology Job Posting Number 2026145NTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department/School Biology Position Description The Department of Biology seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/nontenured faculty to teach. Temporary/nontenured faculty are appointed to teach one to four courses per semester. Teaching appointments are based upon student demand on a semester-by-semester basis. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental/school need. Successful candidates may teach at the San Marcos and Round Rock campuses and/or online, depending on the needs of the academic department. This posting is for the Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer2027 semesters. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration as the need arises. Positions are subject to availability of funds. Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in Biology or a closely related life science field. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience teaching undergraduate courses as the instructor of record Application Procedures The department will accept applications from qualified applicants on a continual basis. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered, https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57389 . Interested applicants should submit the following materials: A cover Letter. A curriculum Vitae. A letter of Teaching Philosophy. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting universities. Type of Position Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time Proposed Start Date Posting Date 06/24/2026 Review Date 06/01/2027 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact—advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57389 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned PhD in the biological sciences or a related field? Yes, I have an earned PhD in the biological sciences or a related field No, I do not have an earned PhD in the biological sciences or a related field Yes, ABD with a completion date prior to start date * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are delivered face-to-face, online, or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * What is your schedule availability?  Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Fall, Spring, Summer, or Combination? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58242": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | HR Business Partner Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student HR Business Partner Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026725 Posting/Functional Title HR Business Partner University Pay Plan Title HR Business Partner Location San Marcos Department Human Resources Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary commensurate with experience Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Required Qualifications Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the following qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in human resource management, Organizational Development, Business Administration or related field. A minimum of three (3) years of Human Resources experience providing guidance and consultation to internal customers/business managers on employee relations and performance management, with exposure to working with compensation, talent acquisition, learning/development, organizational development, benefits, and HRIS is required. Knowledge of federal and state employment laws and HR best practices. Understanding of core human resources functions including employee relations, talent acquisition, compensation, organizational development, performance management, learning and development, HRIS , and employee engagement. Experience using HR systems, data management tools, and technology to support HR operations and decision-making. Strong relationship-building, consulting, and communication skills with the ability to effectively partner with leaders and employees at all levels. Demonstrated critical thinking, problem-solving, conflict resolution, and decision-making abilities. Ability to analyze and interpret workforce data, trends, and metrics to support business and organizational objectives. Experience managing multiple priorities and providing strategic HR guidance in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and proactively identify and address organizational needs. Strong collaboration skills with the ability to build effective partnerships across departments and HR functional areas. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, HR systems, and other digital tools, including emerging AI technologies. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in human resources, Business Administration, Organizational Development, or a related field. Professional HR certification ( PHR , SPHR , SHRM -CP, SHRM - SCP , or equivalent). Previous experience in higher education or a public-sector environment. Job Description Responsible for aligning business objectives with HR strategies/services by serving as a consultant to leadership and employees. Acts as a liaison between supported divisions/departments and HR specialty functions to ensure that HR solutions are aligned with institutional priorities. Job Duties Duties Manage and resolve complex employee relations matters and workplace concerns with professionalism, sound judgment, and a solutions-oriented approach. Provide day-to-day guidance and coaching to managers related to performance management, employee development, disciplinary actions, and workplace issues. Partner closely with leadership and employees to foster positive working relationships, strengthen employee engagement, and support productivity and retention efforts. Advise departments on HR policies, procedures, and best practices while identifying opportunities for process improvement and operational effectiveness. Participate in regular meetings with division and department leadership to provide strategic HR consultation and support. Support organizational initiatives including workforce planning, succession planning, departmental restructures, and talent management strategies. Collaborate with Compensation and Classification teams on position reviews, updates, and compensation-related considerations to ensure alignment with institutional practices and market standards. Partner with Talent Acquisition on recruitment strategies, key searches, and hiring initiatives to attract and retain top talent. Identify learning and development opportunities for departments and leaders and collaborate with HR partners to support training and coaching initiatives. Analyze workforce trends, metrics, and organizational data to recommend HR solutions, programs, and process improvements. Perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 08/11/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58118 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum of 3 years of HR experience providing guidance and consultation support to leadership and employees, with experience in at least 2 HR disciplines such as Compensation, Talent Acquisition, Learning & Development, HRIS, ER, Performance Management, or Benefits? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57826": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Nontenure Faculty Pool – Health and Human Performance Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Nontenure Faculty Pool – Health and Human Performance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Nontenure Faculty Pool – Health and Human Performance Job Posting Number 2027016NTL Job Location Round Rock, San Marcos, Other - Collin County College/Division College of Education Department/School Dept of Health & Human Performance Position Description The Department of Health and Human Performance seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/non-tenured faculty to teach in athletic training, exercise and sports science, physical fitness and wellness, public health, recreational therapy, and recreation and sport management. Temporary/nontenured faculty are appointed to teach one to two courses per semester. Teaching appointments are based on student demand on a semester-by-semester basis. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental needs. Successful candidates may teach at the San Marcos, Round Rock, or Collin County campuses and/or online, depending on the needs of the academic department. This posting is for the fall 2026, spring 2027, and summer 2027 semesters. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Required Qualifications Specific educational requirements vary by position, but a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field is generally required. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience is preferred. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57769 . Interested individuals should submit: A current CV. A cover letter. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant’s skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting universities Type of Position Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time Proposed Start Date Posting Date 07/15/2026 Review Date 05/31/2027 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact—advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57769 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field? Yes, I hold a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field. No, I do not have a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field * Are you a current Texas State University employee? Yes No * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are fully online or delivered remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Fall, Spring, Summer or Combination? (Open Ended Question) * What is your schedule availability? Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the specific program area(s) for which you wish to be considered:\r\n•\tAthletic Training\r\n•\tExercise and Sports Science\r\n•\tPhysical Fitness and Wellness\r\n•\tPublic Health\r\n•\tRecreational Therapy\r\n•\tRecreation and Sport Management Althletic Training Exercise and Sports Science Physical Fitness and Wellness Public Health Recreational Therapy Recreation and Sport Managment Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
