    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58370": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Graphic Designer Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Graphic Designer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026770 Posting/Functional Title Graphic Designer University Pay Plan Title Graphic Designer Location San Marcos Department VP Student Success Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $4,002-$4,876 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Bachelor’s degree in visual design, communication, graphic design, advertising, or a closely related field. Demonstrated knowledge of design principles and applications for print and digital media. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite or comparable design software. Knowledge of advertising, branding, and campaign development. Strong skills in project and process management, including managing multiple concurrent design requests and deadlines. Proficiency with computers and common office and design technologies, including printers, photo and video equipment, and basic UX concepts. Effective oral and written communication skills, with the ability to communicate professionally with a diverse range of stakeholders. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with both professional staff and student employees. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field (e.g., communication, graphic design, advertising, or visual design). Experience working in a higher education or student affairs environment. Experience supervising student employees or managing small creative teams. Experience presenting workshops or trainings on design, media, or marketing topics. Familiarity with work request and project management systems, including tracking, prioritization, and reporting. Demonstrated ability to align creative work with institutional branding, strategic goals, and assessment data. Job Description The Graphic Designer position produces high-quality visual design for print, digital, video, and web to support the Division of Student Success and its programs, services, and initiatives. The role ensures consistent application of university and divisional brand standards across all departments, serving as a key steward of the visual identity and advising departments on effective design practices. The position manages a broad range of projects from concept through delivery, balancing multiple deadlines while aligning all materials with the mission and vision of the Division of Student Success. The Graphic Designer works under the direction of the Director of Marketing and Communications, collaborates closely with campus partners, and will supervise and mentor student workers involved in design, media, and production tasks. Job Duties Design and Creative Production Conceptualize and design visual materials for print, digital, web, and video to support Division of Student Success initiatives. Develop concepts and layouts from initial idea through final deliverables, ensuring designs are clear, accessible, and audience-focused. Select format, typography, color, imagery, and overall layout, and edits content within designs for clarity and impact. Create and maintain templates and reusable assets to streamline production and reduce one-off requests. Brand Stewardship and Visual Strategy Apply and uphold university and divisional brand standards across all materials to ensure a consistent visual identity. Align design projects with the mission, vision, and strategic priorities of the Division of Student Success. Recommend appropriate channels and mediums (print, digital, web, social, video) to maximize effectiveness and reach. Advise staff on best practices for visual communication, including image use, readability, and inclusive design. Collaboration and Consultation Collaborate with stakeholders to clarify project goals, audiences, timelines, and deliverables. Conduct project intake, communicate status and timelines, and incorporate feedback while maintaining design quality and brand alignment. Provide guidance or training on topics such as design basics, branding, and effective use of media and visual assets. Build and maintain positive working relationships with staff and student employees to support a collaborative, service-oriented environment. Project and Team Management Manage multiple concurrent design requests, tracking, prioritizing, and scheduling work according to divisional priorities and deadlines. Maintain organized shared repositories of design files, templates, assets, and photography for reference and reuse. Provide day-to-day direction and feedback to student workers on design and media projects, ensuring quality and consistency. Support special projects and other assigned duties, including event-related design needs and rapid-turnaround requests. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 09/02/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) 09/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58363 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Portfolio Optional Documents Media File DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelors' degree? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree or a master's degree in visual design, communication, graphic design, advertising, or a closely related field? No Yes - Bachelor's Degree in visual design, communication, graphic design, advertising, or a closely related field. Yes - Master's Degree in visual design, communication, graphic design, advertising, or a closely related field * How many years of graphic design experience do you have? 0-1 year 2-3 years 4+ years * Do you have working knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite including Photoshop, Premiere, & InDesign? Yes No * Do you have experience in photography, video production, video editing, and/or graphic design? Yes No * What is your level of experience developing marketing assets such as digital signs, websites, print or social media? No experience Beginner Intermediate Advanced * Do you have experience working in a higher education setting? Yes No * Do you have experience leading and supervising student staff? Yes No * Do you have experience of managing multiple projects simultaneously? Yes No * Do you have experience developing and presenting staff training? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57197": {
      "title": "Grant Director- McNair Scholars",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Grant Director- McNair Scholars Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Grant Director- McNair Scholars Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a cover letter that addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications in the order in which they are listed in this job posting. Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026551 Posting/Functional Title Grant Director- McNair Scholars University Pay Plan Title Grant Director, Non-Faculty Location San Marcos Department McNair Scholars Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Grant Monthly Salary $5,000.00 - $6,250.00 Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Doctoral degree in higher education administration, student development, counseling, social work, or STEM -related field. Experience in collegiate teaching, administration, scholarly activities, developing research materials, or working with academic support programs to promote graduate school enrollment and doctoral degree attainment. Knowledge of higher education academic programs, research, and scholarly activities. Experience with academic support programs, or other student support services; Experience advising students on academics, financial aid, college and career preparation. Experience planning, coordinating, and implementing services for college students. Experience managing programs, budgets, staff, and processes. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of TRIO or other higher education academic programs and support services and effective practices supporting student recruitment, retention, and development. Three (3) years of experience in staff supervision, budget management, program development and evaluation, reporting, and compliance with federal regulations. Five (5) years of experience in collegiate teaching, administration, scholarly activities, developing research materials, or working with academic support programs to promote graduate school enrollment and doctoral degree attainment. 2 years program management experience including fiscal management, database management, and staff supervision. Bilingual (Spanish) speaking/writing. Experience working with SAP /Excel for budgets and financial processes. Job Description This is a grant funded position. Continuation of this position is contingent upon grant funding. The Director is responsible for the daily operation and facilitation of the programmatic and administrative components of the McNair Scholars program. The Director will be responsible for coordinating and providing administrative oversight for all phases of the Program. Primary duties involve implementation of program activities and services to meet specific program objectives. Main office location at the Texas State University Campus in San Marcos, Texas. Evening and weekend work may be required. Job Duties Responsible for the daily operation of the program and all components associated with the program. Conduct regularly scheduled group and individual meetings with program staff. Prepare and administer program budget in accordance with federal and university budgetary policies and procedures. Develop and implement strategies to meet program objectives. Maintain relevant data and metrics on performance to measure and evaluate goals and objectives. Develop and maintain processes for keeping accurate records. Monitor file/record keeping schedule in accordance with university guidelines. Conduct regularly schedule reviews of participant files and financial information. Communicate and correspond with Department of Education Program officers on program performance (annual report), annual budgets, program needs, requests, progress updates and questions. Work with university departments to resolve any issues that may arise as they pertain to budgets, financial analysis, reconciliations, procurement, travel, the hiring process, office maintenance or otherwise. Attend State, Regional and National Conferences. Other duties as assigned. Additional Information to Applicants Please include a cover letter that addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications in the order in which they are listed in this job posting. Job Open Date 05/28/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Applicant must have a valid Texas Driver's License and be a driver in good standing with less than ten (10) points deducted for driving infractions as determined by the employer driving standards system. Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the United States. The University will not sponsor or assume sponsorship of any candidate requiring a petition for a H1B employment visa. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57139 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58065": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Head Plumber Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Head Plumber Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Must be available and willing to work after hours, on-call duty on a rotating basis with other shop personnel. This position requires driving University vehicles. Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026703 Posting/Functional Title Head Plumber University Pay Plan Title Head Plumber Location San Marcos Department Facilities Operations Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $4,483.00 - $5,306.08 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Valid Texas Journeyman [or higher] Plumber license Valid Backflow license or be able to obtain one in 180 days Plumbing experience and knowledge of plumbing concepts, codes and laws; EPA regulations, safety procedures and regulations; repair and maintenance of all types of plumbing fixtures and their apparatus. Experience working independently and as part of a team troubleshooting and correcting plumbing challenges, including emergency responses. Available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel Preferred Qualifications Master Plumber license Previous employment experience as a plumber (or equivalent) in government and/or higher education environment Experience with AiM (Assetworks) Integrated Work Management System Job Description Responsible for providing emergency response to maintenance oriented calls or plumbing emergencies across all campus facilities. Job Duties Maintain and operate heavy equipment. Repair water and sewer lines pumps, faucets, water closets, tubs, showers, water heaters on emergency basis, as needed. Train and mentor other plumbing shop personnel Unstop clogged water closets, urinals, sinks, bathtubs, shower and floor drains, and sewers; repair water, gas, and sewer lines; repair/replace laboratory faucets, traps, and sinks; and repair/replace hose bibs; and test and repair backflow devices. Unclog storm and roof drains. Repair, replace, varied plumbing fixtures on campus. Construct, remove or rough-in fixtures in varied campus bldg., properties. Install or maintain various water, gas, air, sewer, as needed, at various campus facilities. Complete daily mileage, work logs and requisition parts, materials, personnel. Complete electronic work logs and requisition parts, materials, personnel. Complies with all state and university policies. Works various schedules and required to be on call. Required to carry a cell phone. Operate a university vehicle. Perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information to Applicants Must be available and willing to work after hours, on-call duty on a rotating basis with other shop personnel. This position requires driving University vehicles. Job Open Date 07/27/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 7:30AM Normal Work Hours End 4:30PM Posting Notices Applicant must have a valid Texas Driver's License and be a driver in good standing with less than ten (10) points deducted for driving infractions as determined by the employer driving standards system. Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57214 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation #1 DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently hold or have the ability to obtain a drivers license within 90 days of employment? Yes No * Are you available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel? Yes No * The minimum requirement for this position is a Texas Journeyman plumbing license. Do you have a valid license? Yes No * The minimum requirement for this position is a Backflow license. Do you have a valid Backflow license or are you able to obtain one in 180 days? Yes Will be able to obtain one within 180 days. No * Do you currently hold a valid Master Plumber license? Yes No * Do you have previous employment experience as a plumber in a government and/or higher education environment? Yes No * What level of proficiency using the AiM (AssetWorks) platform do you have? Advanced experience/proficiency Intermediate experience/proficiency Little to no experience/proficiency Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
