    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58297": {
      "title": "Financial Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Financial Operations Specialist Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Financial Operations Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship or transfer. Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026750 Posting/Functional Title Financial Operations Specialist University Pay Plan Title Admin Financial Analyst Location San Marcos Department VP for Information Technology Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $5,624.00 + commensurate with experience Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Knowledge of financial operations principles and frameworks, including cost allocation, budgeting, forecasting, optimization, and financial accountability. Knowledge of cloud financial management and pricing models, including consumption-based billing, reserved capacity, savings plans, commitments, licensing, and other cloud cost-management concepts. Understanding of cloud infrastructure, including compute, storage, networking, databases, software licensing, and other technology services, sufficient to interpret cost drivers and spending patterns. Skill in analyzing and reconciling financial and cloud consumption data, identifying cost trends and anomalies, developing forecasts, preparing reports and dashboards, and recommending opportunities for cost optimization. Ability to work collaboratively across organizational functions, manage multiple priorities, communicate effectively, organize complex financial and technical information, and provide recommendations to management and stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications FinOps or cloud-related certifications. Experience using cloud cost-management, optimization, reporting, or dashboarding tools. Job Description The FinOps Specialist performs financial operations and cloud cost management activities in support of the IT Division. This position works collaboratively with IT Finance, IT Procurement, and Central Systems Operations and is responsible for monitoring and analyzing cloud expenditures, usage, budgets, forecasts, billing, and financial performance to promote cost transparency, accountability, and efficient use of cloud resources. Job Duties Monitor and analyze cloud usage, costs, budgets, forecasts, and financial performance to identify trends, anomalies, optimization opportunities, and potential budget impacts, while developing and maintaining cost models and financial reports to support organizational planning and decision-making. Review and reconcile cloud invoices, billing data, purchase orders, contracts, and financial records; investigate discrepancies and coordinate their resolution with the appropriate departments and vendors. Develop and maintain cost allocation, tagging, chargeback, and cost management methodologies to accurately assign cloud expenditures to departments, applications, projects, and other organizational units. Identify and recommend cloud cost optimization opportunities, including resource rightsizing, elimination of unused resources, commitment-based discounts, licensing optimization, and improvements to cloud architecture and consumption practices. Track cost savings, cost avoidance, utilization, and other FinOps performance measures; prepare reports and dashboards to communicate financial performance and optimization results. Collaborate with Finance, Procurement, and Central Systems Operations to establish cloud budgets, manage expenditures, improve forecasting, and promote financial accountability. Assist with the development, implementation, and maintenance of FinOps policies, procedures, standards, controls, and governance practices for cloud financial management. Perform related duties and special projects as assigned. Additional Information to Applicants Please note this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship or transfer. Job Open Date 08/26/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57755 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation #1 DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Letter of Recommendation #2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56220": {
      "title": "Temporary Positions - Technician",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Temporary Positions - Technician Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Temporary Positions - Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Departments will access this job posting to search for applicants to fill Non-Student Non-Regular (NSNR) positions at the University. Non-student, non-regular staff may work on short assignments or intermittently throughout the year, but the total hours worked must not exceed 19.75 hours per week. This position is temporarily funded. Employment is contingent on funding availability. Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026356 Posting/Functional Title Temporary Positions - Technician University Pay Plan Title Temporary Worker- Technician Location Round Rock, San Marcos Department Human Resources Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Temporary Funding Source Temporary Monthly Salary Varies Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Preferred Qualifications Job Description What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas,, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building. Job Duties Occupations that require a combination of basic scientific or technical knowledge and manual skills which can be obtained through specialized post-secondary school education or equivalent on-the-job training. Technician occupations include computer programmers, drafters, surveyors, licensed practical nurses, photographers, radio operators, technical illustrators, highway technicians, technicians (medical, dental, electronic, physical sciences), police and fire sergeants, inspectors (production or processing inspectors, testers and weighers), kindred workers. Texas State Technician title examples: Medical Technologist; Lab Services Tech; Child Care Teacher Additional Information to Applicants Departments will access this job posting to search for applicants to fill Non-Student Non-Regular ( NSNR ) positions at the University. Non-student, non-regular staff may work on short assignments or intermittently throughout the year, but the total hours worked must not exceed 19.75 hours per week. This position is temporarily funded. Employment is contingent on funding availability. Job Open Date 03/02/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56219 Applicant Document Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications List of References Additional Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
