    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57765": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice in Marketing",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Practice in Marketing Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Practice in Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Practice in Marketing Job Posting Number 2027006NTL Job Location San Marcos, Other - Online College/Division McCoy College of Business Department/School Department of Marketing Position Description This position requires effective teaching in the Online DBA program, with a primary emphasis on qualitative research methods. The successful candidate will contribute to doctoral education by teaching courses that support applied business research and evidence-based decision making, including instruction in qualitative research design, data collection, and data analysis. Beyond research methods, the successful candidate may contribute to core DBA courses such as Global Business Issues, Strategic Marketing Analysis and Applications, and others as needed. The candidate should also be prepared to teach other relevant courses at the graduate or undergraduate level as departmental needs arise. Experience with online or asynchronous instructional delivery is strongly recommended. The position requires maintaining currency and relevance in the candidate’s areas of teaching and research, including research methods and applied business disciplines, through ongoing engagement with current research, industry practices, and emerging technologies, including advancements in artificial intelligence. The position also requires providing service to students, the department, the profession, and the university. Responsibilities may include mentoring doctoral students, supporting their professional development and dissertation work, and contributing to the continued growth of the DBA program. This position includes an optional opportunity to serve as Director of the DBA Program. The primary responsibility of the position remains teaching in the Online DBA program. Candidates who express interest in the Director role may be considered for a course release and opportunities for administrative experience. Required Qualifications A terminal degree ( DBA or PhD) in business or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution. At least five years of experience in a professional, academic, or applied research role. Demonstrated expertise in qualitative research methods and their application in business or organizational contexts. The successful candidate must be qualified as a Practice Academic (PA) or Scholarly Practitioner (SP) in accordance with AACSB and Texas State University standards (available at https://www.mccoy.txst.edu/faculty-staff/faculty-resources/policies-procedures/college/cbapps-5-07.html ). Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience in graduate or doctoral-level programs. Experience with qualitative data analysis software (e.g., NVivo, ATLAS .ti, MAXQDA ). Experience with online or hybrid teaching environments and asynchronous instructional design. Familiarity with quantitative research approaches and experience conducting applied research in business or organizational contexts. Demonstrated engagement with industry, executive education, or applied research settings. Content Breadth: Ability to contribute to DBA curriculum areas such as global business, strategic marketing, etc. Leadership Potential: Interest in or experience with academic program leadership and/or graduate program leadership, including curriculum development, accreditation processes (e.g., AACSB ), or managing stakeholder relationships. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered, https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57590 . The confidential review of credentials will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit the following before August 15, 2026 : Cover letter addressing required and preferred qualifications. Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (All in one document, from all degree granting institutions). The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting Universities. The Department of Marketing is not able to provide visa sponsorship for this position. The proposed start date is 1/1/2027, but there is a second option to start on 8/15/2027. Salary will be commensurate with experience. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Date 07/08/2026 Review Date 08/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact—advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57590 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a terminal degree (DBA or a PhD) in business or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution? Yes, I have a DBA from an AACSB-accredited institution. Yes, I have a PhD from an AACSB-accredited institution. No, I do not have a DBA or a PhD from an AACSB-accredited institution. * Would you be interested in serving as DBA Director, as a secondary responsibility in this role? Yes No * Do you now or will you in the future require a petition for a H1B employment visa? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58388": {
      "title": "Assistant NCAA Certification Officer",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant NCAA Certification Officer Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant NCAA Certification Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026771 Posting/Functional Title Assistant NCAA Certification Officer University Pay Plan Title Ast NCAA Certification Officer Location San Marcos Department Athletic Certification Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $3,662.31 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Experience independently researching materials to compile, develop and summarize for professional reports on a frequent or recurring basis. Experience analyzing information, identifying problems, defining alternatives, and developing recommendations for administrators. Experience interpreting and applying rules, regulations, and laws regarding student records. Evidence of the ability to work independently and as a team member. Documented experience communicating orally and in writing with varied stakeholders. High School Diploma. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Documented experience working with NCAA regulations (Bylaw 14) related to athletic academic eligibility. Experience in evaluating and interpreting degree plans and curriculum, preferably utilizing Degree Works degree audit system. Experience working in the Banner Student Information System environment. Experience working with the NCAA Eligibility Center website and NCAA Academic Portal. Experience working with Teamworks. Knowledge of Texas State’s undergraduate core curriculum and degree program requirements. Job Description The Assistant NCAA Athletics Certification Officer is responsible for assisting the NCAA Athletics Certification Officer in obtaining, evaluating, and documenting the academic credentials in accordance with National Collegiate Athletics Association ( NCAA ) and conference eligibility rules for approximately 400+ student-athletes. Job Duties Eligibility Worksheets – Update and monitor individual SA eligibility worksheets and team eligibility worksheets on a continuous basis. Provide feedback and projections regarding NCAA eligibility to Athletics Academic Center in a timely manner. Certify Student-Athletes for Competition – Review the academic credentials for each SA to determine eligibility status. Assimilate and file appropriate documentation to support certification (i.e. NCAA SA Details Report, transcripts, degree audits, academic progress forms, etc.). Create EDF and submit to Athletics Compliance Office. Academic Pre-Evaluations – Conduct an academic pre-evaluations for prospective student-athletes and provide accurate and timely feedback to the Athletics Compliance Office. Academic Performance Program – Assist the NCAA Certification Officer in updating Compliance Assistant 2.0 with pertinent information for the APP (including APR and GSR ) each year. Work cooperatively with Athletics Academic Center staff and the Athletics Compliance staff to ensure information is accurate. Provide feedback for any NCAA responses to information. Academic Progress Forms – Create, distribute, review, compile and file the academic progress forms from the College Advising centers. Follow up with each College Advising center in a timely manner for clarification when needed. Full-Time Enrollment Monitoring – Oversee the monitoring of full-time enrollment of SAs, managers, male practice players and graduate assistants. Other Assigned Duties – Assist the NCAA Athletic Compliance Officer with general office organization and support. Professionalism – Appearance, attendance, punctuality, and office decorum met Registrar’s office and University policies consistently. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 09/04/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58322 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience conducting an academic pre-evaluation for prospective student athletes? Yes No * Do you have experience with creating, distributing, reviewing, and compiling the file on academic progress forms from the College Advising centers. Follow up with each College Advising center in a timely manner for clarification when needed. Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57257": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Nontenure Faculty Pool - Curriculum and Instruction Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Nontenure Faculty Pool - Curriculum and Instruction Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Nontenure Faculty Pool - Curriculum and Instruction Job Posting Number 2026135NTL Job Location Round Rock, San Marcos, Other - Collin College - McKinney, TX College/Division College of Education Department/School Curriculum And Instruction Position Description The Department of Curriculum and Instruction seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/nontenured faculty to teach Bilingual-Bicultural Education, Early Childhood Education, Educational Technology, Elementary Education, Middle Level Education, Postsecondary Student Success, Reading Education, Secondary Education, Special Education, and Talent Development. Temporary/nontenured faculty are appointed to teach one to four courses per semester. Teaching appointments are based upon student demand on a semester-by-semester basis. Eligibility for reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental need. Successful candidates may teach at the San Marcos campus, Round Rock campus, Collin College (McKinney, TX), PK-12 school/school district field sites, and/or online, depending on the needs of the academic department. This posting is for the 2026-2027 academic year. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Required Qualifications Specific educational requirements vary by position, but a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field is generally required. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience is preferred. Application Procedures Applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57203 . The Department of Curriculum and Instruction will accept applications from qualified applicants on a continual basis. Interested individuals should submit the following materials: Current CV. Letter of interest outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for appointment. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant’s skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Type of Position Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time Proposed Start Date Posting Date 06/02/2026 Review Date 05/31/2027 Close Date Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact—advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57203 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field? Yes, I hold a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field. No, I do not have a minimum of a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in the teaching field * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are delivered face-to-face, online, or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the specific program area(s) for which you wish to be considered: Bilingual-Bicultural Education Early Childhood Education Educational Technology Elementary Education Elementary Education - Literacy Elementary Education - Math Elementary Education - Science Elementary Education - Social Studies Middle Level Education Postsecondary Student Success Secondary Education Reading Education Special Education Talent Development * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Fall, Spring, Summer or Combination? (Open Ended Question) * What is your schedule availability?  Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
