    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57692": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Facilities & Grounds",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, Facilities &amp; Grounds Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Director, Facilities & Grounds Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position may require driving university vehicles Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026642 Posting/Functional Title Assistant Director, Facilities & Grounds University Pay Plan Title Asst Dir, Campus Recreation Location San Marcos Department Campus Recreation Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $4,750.00 - $5,000.00 Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Minimum of two years of professional work experience within facility operations (e.g. Campus Recreation, Fitness, Aquatics, Outdoors, etc.) or related field Bachelor’s degree in Recreation, Exercise Science, Health Education, Sport Management, Turf Management, Higher Education, or related field Progressively responsible experience within campus recreation or related field. Current CPR , AED , First Aid and or ability to obtain within 45 days Preferred Qualifications Experience supervising full time staff in a higher education setting Master’s degree in Recreation, Exercise Science, Health Education, Sport Management, Turf Management, Higher Education, or related field In-depth knowledge of turfgrass species, cultivation practices, soil science, irrigation systems, pest management, and turf equipment operation Current Texas Department of Agriculture Pesticide Applicator License Job Description The Assistant Director of Facilities and Grounds will lead and manage the administration and operation of the Facilities program, consisting of all Campus Recreation special events, Grounds Operations, Custodial Operations and Building Maintenance Operations in the pursuit of inspiring Bobcats to be their best and create lasting memories. The Assistant Director will also be responsible for the development and oversight of an 8-person Custodial team, two Maintenance Worker II positions, and a 5-person Grounds crew. Job Duties Facility Management/Maintenance, Turf Maintenance: 30% Develop and manage a diverse Facilities program including the administration of all campus recreation grounds operations, custodial operations and building maintenance operations. Oversee the daily facility activities, including custodial, maintenance, repairs and safety inspections on facility systems, including HVAC , plumbing, electrical and structural components. Oversee the preparation and upkeep of sports fields, including mowing, fertilization and pest control to ensure optimal playing conditions. Oversee work order and asset management tracking systems. Implement innovative ideas that align with strategic plan and department priorities to improve overall operations and growth of programs/services/usage. Develop and conduct assessments of program goals annually. Report assessment results to leadership as documentation of programmatic outcomes supporting department and division goals. Staff Development and Oversight: 30% Oversee the development and performance evaluation of an 8-person Custodial team, two Maintenance Worker II positions, and a 5-person Grounds crew. Meet with full time staff regularly to discuss program goals, professional goals and area updates. Develop and oversee staff schedules and project lists to ensure timely completion and tracking. With the potential to hire, train, supervise, and evaluate approximately 5 student staff. Administration and Budget Development: 20% Lead annual budget development process in collaboration with Coordinator, Maintenance Worker II and Grounds crew. Plan, prepare and manage program budgets including overseeing income projections and monitoring income, expenses, and yearly comparisons. Purchase equipment and supplies. Approve staff time and ensure compliance with payroll and purchasing processes. Risk Management and Safety: 10% Ensure staff compliance with industry standard safety and risk management practices, facility and equipment inspections, and established Campus Recreation policies and procedures. Knowledge of applicable regulations, environmental guidelines, and safety standards governing turf management practices. Familiarity with pesticide regulations, water conservation measures, and environmental sustainability initiatives. Other Duties: 10% Actively participate in departmental programs and projects designed to support the mission and goals of the university, division, and department. Serve on committees and task forces, as assigned. Other duties as requested or required, whether or not specifically mentioned in this job description. This position requires a flexible work schedule which at times will require frequent attendance during evenings and weekends. Additional hours may be required during peak periods. Additional Information to Applicants This position may require driving university vehicles Job Open Date 07/02/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57613 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold an earned Bachelor’s degree in Recreation, Exercise Science, Health Education, Sport Management, Higher Education, or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of professional work experience in campus recreation or a related field? Yes, I have a minimum of 2 years of experience Less than 2 years of experience No Experience in Campus Recreation or related field * Do you hold a Master's Degree in Recreation, Exercise Science, Health Education, Sport Management or Higher Education. Yes No * Do you have In-depth knowledge of turfgrass species, cultivation practices, soil science, irrigation systems, pest management, and turf equipment operation? Yes Some Knowledge No Knowledge or Experience * Do you hold current CPR, AED, First Aid certifications and or have the ability to obtain within 45 days of hire? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
