    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58448": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology Job Posting Number 2027010TTL Job Location San Marcos Department Psychology Position Description The Department of Psychology at Texas State University is seeking a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology. Expertise in aging is preferred (although all specializations in clinical psychology will be considered). The successful Assistant Professor candidate will be expected to: 1) develop and maintain an active research program that incorporates both undergraduate and graduate students; 2) teach undergraduate- and graduate-level courses relevant to clinical psychology; 3) supervise graduate theses/dissertations; 4) actively seek and maintain external funding; 5) have or obtain licensure to practice clinical psychology in the state of Texas and maintain licensure; and 6) participate in service as a good departmental citizen. Required Qualifications PhD in Clinical Psychology at the time of appointment. Scholarship productivity and record of scholarly publications (evaluated in relation to time since completion of the doctoral degree). Evidence of, or potential for, incorporating students into the research program. Licensed or license eligible in the state of Texas Preferred Qualifications Specialization in aging (although all specializations in clinical psychology will be considered). Evidence of, or potential for, securing external research funding. Quality collegiate teaching experience. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58290 . Please submit the following by October 15, 2026: Cover letter. Current curriculum vitae. Statement addressing applicant’s qualifications and research interests. Representative publications. Statement of teaching philosophy. Evidence of teaching effectiveness. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide insight into your skills and experiences. Please include the names and email addresses for your references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 10/15/2026 Close Date 10/15/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact—advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58290 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Examples of Recent Publications Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No, I do not have a Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58451": {
      "title": "Senior Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Senior Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Senior Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please make sure your resume addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications. Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026691 Posting/Functional Title Senior Administrative Assistant University Pay Plan Title Sr Admin Asst Location San Marcos Department Dean of Students Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $4,002 - $4,583.33 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. High school diploma or GED . Four (4) years of progressively responsible administrative support experience, including at least two (2) years providing direct support to senior leaders, executives, or managers. Experience coordinating complex calendars, meetings, and multiple competing priorities. Experience preparing, editing, and proofreading professional correspondence, reports, and presentations. Experience handling confidential and sensitive information with discretion and professionalism. Experience supporting financial and/or human resources administrative processes, including purchasing, travel, budgeting, or personnel documentation. Experience using Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and the ability to learn and adapt to new software systems and technologies. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Demonstrated organizational, time management, and customer service skills with exceptional attention to detail. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree. Experience providing executive-level administrative support in higher education, government, or a similarly complex organization. Experience supporting budget, procurement, human resources, or business operations. Experience using enterprise systems such as (outlined TXST system) ERP , financial, human resources, records management, or scheduling platforms. Experience coordinating projects, events, committees, or special initiatives involving multiple stakeholders. Job Description The Senior Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive executive-level administrative support to multiple Associate Vice Presidents within the Division of Student Success. Serving as a strategic partner, this position manages executives, calendars, coordinates administrative operations, supports budget and personnel processes, and facilitates effective communication across the division and university. The role requires exceptional organizational skills, professionalism, discretion, and independent judgment in handling sensitive information and competing priorities. The Senior Administrative Assistant proactively anticipates executive needs, resolves operational challenges, improves processes, and ensures timely completion of executive priorities. Job Duties Executive Administration and Executive Support Manage complex calendars for Associate Vice Presidents, prioritizing competing demands and ensuring the effective use of executive time. Coordinate executive meetings, travel, conferences, and related logistics while anticipating needs and resolving scheduling challenges. Prepare agendas, briefing materials, reports, and supporting documentation for meetings, events, and executive decision-making. Monitor executive priorities, commitments, deadlines, and action items to ensure timely follow-through. Exercise independent judgment in managing communications, requests, and matters requiring executive attention. Support executive initiatives and special projects through coordination, follow-up, and stakeholder engagement. Administrative Operations, Communication, and Project Management Draft, edit, proofread, and distribute executive correspondence, reports, presentations, policies, memoranda, and other official communications. Coordinate executive and divisional meetings by scheduling participants, preparing materials, documenting outcomes, and tracking action items. Develop, maintain, and improve administrative procedures, templates, and workflows that promote operational efficiency and consistency. Research, compile, and organize information, reports, and data to support executive decision-making and strategic planning efforts. Business Operations Support budget, procurement, and financial operations through purchasing, payment processing, reconciliations, travel expense reporting, and financial recordkeeping. Monitor expenditures and budget activity, identify discrepancies, and communicate concerns or recommendations to leadership. Provide administrative support for recruitment, onboarding, personnel actions, leave administration, training coordination, and other human resources processes. Maintain administrative tracking systems for contracts, renewals, purchases, personnel actions, compliance requirements, and key deadlines. Coordinate vendor, contract, and purchasing activities to ensure timely processing and compliance with university procedure Records Management, Compliance, and Accountability Serve as the Records Retention Liaison by maintaining electronic and physical records in compliance with university policies and applicable retention requirements. Safeguard confidential personnel, student, financial, legal, and institutional information while maintaining the highest standards of discretion and professionalism. Monitor administrative records, processes, and documentation to ensure accuracy, completeness, and compliance with university policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements. Maintain current and accurate executive documents, forms, templates, and official communications consistent with university standards. Customer Service, Event Coordination, and Continuous Improvement Serve as a primary point of contact for executive offices, responding professionally to inquiries from students, faculty, staff, parents, community members, and external partners. Coordinate executive-level events, retreats, advisory boards, conferences, and special programs, including logistics, communications, registrations, travel, and on-site support. Utilize Microsoft Office, Adobe Acrobat, enterprise systems, and other university technologies to support executive operations and administrative functions. Identify and implement opportunities to improve efficiency through technology, automation, process improvement, and workflow redesign. Troubleshoot administrative and operational issues, resolving routine matters independently and escalating complex or sensitive issues as appropriate. Foster collaborative relationships and provide high-quality customer service through professionalism, responsiveness, accountability, and initiative. Additional Information to Applicants Please make sure your resume addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications. Job Open Date 09/14/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) 09/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57851 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current Texas State University employee? Yes No * Do you have an Associate or Bachelors' Degree? Yes No * Do you have four (4) years of progressively responsible administrative support experience, including at least two (2) years providing direct support to senior leaders, executives, or managers? No Yes, 4 years of progressively responsible administrative support Yes, 2 of the years providing direct support to senior leaders, executives, or managers. * What level of experience do you have maintaining multiple calendars and coordinating schedules? No experience Basic Scheduling Managing Multiple Calendars Advanced coordination with conflict resolution * Do you have experience working with MS Office, ERP Systems for budget, finance, and human resources? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58456": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design Job Posting Number 2027012TTL Job Location San Marcos Department School of Theatre, Dance, & Film Position Description The School of Theatre, Dance, and Film at Texas State University seeks an Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design (Tenure Track or Professor of Practice), starting fall 2027. The successful candidate will join a nationally recognized department with a dynamic faculty dedicated to a collaborative and immersive approach to teaching graduate and undergraduate students. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teach graduate and undergraduate courses in scenic design and related topics which may include drafting, history, analysis, and graphic skills. Mentor and advise graduate and undergraduate student designers on realized production work. Actively recruit exceptional candidates for the MFA design program. Participate in department production season planning. Collaborate with the Design, Technology, and Management Area in support of current initiatives and new developments. Maintain an active agenda of creative and/or scholarly research including occasional designs for department productions. Provide service to the School, College, and University, commensurate with rank. Required Qualifications Required qualifications for Assistant Professor Rank (Tenure Line): MFA in Theatre Design. Active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. Required qualifications for Associate Professor Rank (Tenure Line): MFA in Theatre Design. Extensive and active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre; minimum of 7 years to be considered for Associate Rank. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. University/college teaching experience. Required qualifications for Assistant Professor of Practice Rank: Bachelor’s degree. Active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre; minimum of 7 years. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. Required qualifications for Associate Professor of Practice Rank: Bachelor’s degree. Extensive and active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre; minimum of 12 years. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. The successful applicant will receive the appropriate rank and title based on university and school established standards. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a secondary design discipline with a preference for costume or projection design. Experience teaching at the graduate and/or undergraduate level. Demonstrated mentorship of graduate students and/or assistant designers. Proven track record of effective collaboration. Experience in non-theatrical applications of design (e.g., themed environment, events). Demonstrated organizational and leadership skills suitable for academic program oversight. Application Procedures The position will remain open until filled. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58372 . For full consideration, applications should be received by October 18, 2026 . A current CV Cover letter that includes your qualifications and fit with the job description. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 10/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact—advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58372 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Artistic Philosophy Digital Files (Personal Creative Works) Statement of Teaching/Mentorship Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Portfolio List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a M.F.A. in Theatre with an emphasis in Technical Production or related field by date of hire? Yes, I have a M.F.A. in Theatre with an emphasis in Technical Production or related field. Yes, anticipated completion of the M.F.A. in Theatre with an emphasis in Technical Production or related field prior to start date. No. * Do you have a Bachelor's degree? yes No * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
