    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58483": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling Job Posting Number 2027016TTL Job Location San Marcos Department Conslng, Ldrship, Adlt Educ & Schl Psych Position Description The Department of Counseling, Leadership, Adult Education, and School Psychology ( CLAS ) in the College of Education at Texas State University, a Hispanic-Serving Institution ( HSI ) located in San Marcos, Texas, invites applications for a tenure-earning assistant professor position of Professional Counseling beginning August 2027. This position is focused on teaching and research in the School Counseling Concentration and involves teaching, research, service, and program support in a vibrant master’s program in Central Texas. Specific responsibilities include teaching courses in Professional Counseling, maintaining an active and productive program of research, engaging in external funding submissions, and providing service to the program, department, university, and profession. Program: The Professional Counseling Program is CACREP -accredited in three specialty areas: Clinical Mental Health Counseling; Marriage, Couple, and Family Counseling; and School Counseling. This position will include teaching core courses in our counseling program, with a particular focus on school counseling courses, Developmental Issues, and Child and Adolescent Counseling. The successful candidate will be headquartered on the main university campus in San Marcos and will teach courses on both the main university campus in San Marcos and at the university’s Round Rock campus. Department: The CLAS Department serves approximately 975 students seeking undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral degrees in Professional Counseling ( COUN ), Educational and Community Leadership ( EDCL ), Adult, Professional, and Community Education ( APCE ), School Psychology ( SPSY ), Student Affairs in Higher Education ( SAHE ), and Integrated Studies ( INTS ). The CLAS Department provides high quality undergraduate and graduate education to promote significant transformational changes in communities, schools, organizations, and institutions locally and globally. Guided by expert faculty who are deeply engaged in innovative research and dedicated to student success, CLAS students grow into leaders and changemakers in schools, communities, and organizations across Texas and beyond. The CLAS Department is proud to be part of a public, Hispanic-Serving Institution that values discovery and impact through research, teaching, and service. University: Founded in 1899 as a small teaching college, Texas State University is now home to over 40,000 students. The university holds a Carnegie classification of Doctoral University-High Research Activity (R2) and is engaged in a strategic plan to attain Doctoral University-Very High Research Activity (R1) by 2027. Texas State University is located along the beautiful San Marcos River. San Marcos is in the center of the innovation corridor, 40 minutes south of Austin and 60 minutes north of San Antonio and is rich in vibrant and eclectic communities. Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in Counselor Education by employment date of August 2027. A demonstrated record of training and experience in school counseling. A record of, or demonstration of the potential for, research and publication at the national and/or international levels. A record of, or demonstration of the potential for, securing external funding for research. A professional clinical license (e.g., Licensed Professional Counselor [ LPC ], Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist [ LMFT ]) or School Counselor certification or a provisional clinical license (e.g., LPC Associate, LMFT Associate) with a plan in place to complete the professional license in the State of Texas within two years. Preferred Qualifications A documented record of securing external funding for research. Experience teaching core courses in a CACREP -accredited program in the teaching areas listed above. Designation as a clinical supervisor (e.g., LPC -S, LMFT -S) and experience providing clinical supervision in an academic and/or clinical setting. A professional certification in play therapy (e.g., Registered Play Therapist [RPT™], Registered Play Therapist Supervisor [ RPT -S™], School- Based Registered Play Therapist [SB-RPT™]). A demonstrated record of training and experience in play therapy. Application Procedures Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58376 . To guarantee full consideration, all application materials must be submitted by October 14, 2026 . Applicants must submit: A letter of interest that specifically addresses the qualifications and responsibilities noted in this posting. Current curriculum vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). Names and contact information (to include phone and email address) of five references. Three reprints of recent publications (optional). Inquiries about this position may be directed to Dr. Jennifer Greene-Rooks, Search Committee Chair, jgreene@txstate.edu. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting institutions. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 10/15/2026 Close Date 10/27/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact—advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58376 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Licensure Certifications Letter of Recommendation #2 Examples of Recent Publications Examples of Recent Publications #2 Examples of Recent Publications #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctorate in counselor education from a CACREP-accredited program or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have an earned doctorate in counselor education from a CACREP-accredited program. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58489": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Living Learning Communities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Coordinator, Living Learning Communities Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Coordinator, Living Learning Communities Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2027004 Posting/Functional Title Coordinator, Living Learning Communities University Pay Plan Title Student Development Specialist II Location San Marcos Department DHRL Administration Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $4002.00 - $4166.67 Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Bachelor’s degree in higher education administration or related field 1 year of full-time work experience in student housing. Preferred Qualifications Master’s Degree Higher Education administration or related field. Previous student or professional experience in College/University setting with a background in Housing & Residential Life or related field. Excellent logistical thinking and creative problem-solving skills. Previous experience with large-scale programming and student programming. Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment. Experience with retention and student success programming. Job Description The Coordinator for Living Learning Communities (LLCs) will work to support the unit and aid in the complete process of the living-learning recruitment cycle and placement. This role will also collaborate with academic units, faculty advisors, and student success services to provide a robust, integrated living-learning experience within the residence halls. The Coordinator for LLCs will manage campus-wide events and engagement opportunities for living-learning community and theme housing, in line with the student success and residential engagement model framework. Additionally, this position will support LLC outreach efforts through initiatives such as Bobcat preview days and various timeline communications and reminders. This position will report to the Assistant Director for Living Learning Communities in the Residential Experience unit within the Department of Housing and Residential Life at Texas State University. Job Duties LLC Recruitment and Management Support the complete process of a living-learning community cycle, including recruitment, placement, and first-year course registration. Collaborate with the Marketing and the Housing Assignments Coordinator to ensure accurate bed counts and LLC spaces. Advise the Living Learning Communities Activities Board and all programmatic initiatives. Endorse and track student completion of the living learning community medallion program. Collaborate with academic colleges and schools to achieve intended outcomes of the program and the university Coordinate individual co-curricular and community development experiences with each community’s faculty and staff team. Community Engagement Initiatives Collaborate with in-community staff for in-person activities, systematic follow-up, and student support. Identify student needs and create strategic large-scale programs to engage LLC /TC students that provide a sense of mattering and belonging. Interpret student engagement data to evaluate community engagement initiatives from an operational and student experience perspective. Support the development of an on-campus returning student model as it relates to community engagement. Unit Administration Respond to emails and calls from residents, potential students, faculty, and staff regarding living learning committee and theme housing options. Assess programs and initiatives to ensure the event optimally achieves goals and success indicators. Collaborate with Communications team for marketing and social media presence. Coordinate with department staff to align engagement data with persistence, academic, and development data. Departmental and Divisional Partnerships Collaborate with Student Learning Assistance Center and LLC student leaders to promote supplemental instruction, tutoring, writing services, and other academic support to learning community students. Assist with student staff recruitment, developing training and ongoing development sessions for paraprofessional staff, professional staff, and faculty related to the LLCs. Collaborate with other Division of Student Success departments to support division and university-wide strategic priorities. Contribute to and actively participate in strategic planning, department goal setting, data/assessment efforts, and determining community staffing priorities and initiatives. Other duties as requested. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 09/14/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) 09/27/2026 Open Until Filled No Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58288 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree in higher education, student affairs, social work, counseling, psychology, or related field? Yes No * Do you have 1 year of full-time experience working in university housing, residence life, or student affairs? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in university housing or student activities, student conduct, or student affairs area? 0-1 1-2 2-3 years 3+ * How many years of experience do you have with program development and oversight, including large-scale campus programming? Less than 1 2 - 3 years 4 or more years * How many years of experience do you have working in an environment of student support and retentions initiatives? 0-1 1-2 2-3 3+ Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58494": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Guest Services",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Coordinator, Guest Services Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Coordinator, Guest Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2027007 Posting/Functional Title Coordinator, Guest Services University Pay Plan Title Coord, Hsg & Residential Life Location San Marcos Department DHRL Administration Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $4,002.00 - $4,166.67 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Bachelor’s Degree Experience working in customer service, hospitality, recruitment, or communications-related fields. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Event Management, Public Admin, Marketing, Communications or related field. Experience with customer response, call center management, and guest services. Experience with leading and designing a tour program experience. Experience with working in Housing and Residential Life. Experience working in a higher education setting. Job Description The Coordinator for Guest Services position will oversee the customer experience in the Department of Housing and Residential Life ( HRL ). This individual will be responsible for the development and oversight of a tour program for prospective students (daily tours, Bobcat Day, summer orientation, and admitted students day, ect), manage the front desk/reception area and call center of the department, and have oversight and responsibility for monitoring, managing, and ensuring the timely response to concerns that are generated through the departmental email address. Job Duties Tours & Guest Services Oversee Housing and Residential Life tour program, including daily tours and special events. Directly manage desk operations and guest interactions at the main Housing and Residential Life reception desk to provide clear, timely, and student success focused messaging. Assist in the management of annual housing fairs, workshops, and information sessions for students. Answer phone, e-mail, screen, or transfer calls; take messages; refer to other offices as appropriate. Communicate with other personnel, faculty, staff, students, parents, customers and/or others the most up-to-date housing information to ensure quality customer service. Supervision Provide day-to-day supervision and support of a staff of Housing Ambassador (HA) student staff to ensure proper support, training, and response to customers at the desk. Directly oversee and manage staff-wide meetings, one-on-one meetings, and other interactions with student staff to provide maximum support and direction to execute community goals. Hire, train, schedule, and supervise a staff of student housing ambassadors. Evaluate performance of student employees, including ongoing performance management and conduct performance evaluations to support their professional development. Prepare in advance of and actively participate in emergency responses during major events to ensure timely coverage and communication to staff regarding front desk operations. Departmental Responsibilities Represent TXST and HRL at presentations and interact with parents, students, faculty, and other customers. Actively participate in departmental programs and projects designed to support the mission and goals of the department, division, and institution. Assisting the communications team in developing interdepartmental communications and marketing materials. Team in developing interdepartmental communications and marketing materials. Other duties as assigned. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 09/15/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) 09/28/2026 Open Until Filled No Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58359 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you earned a bachelor's degree? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have working in customer service, hospitality, recruitment, or communications-related fields? 0-1 years 2 years 3 years 4 years +5 years * Do you have a master’s degree in Event Management, Public Admin, Marketing, Communications or related field? Yes No * How many years of experience with customer response, call center management, and guest services? 0-1 Years 2 Years 3 Years 4 Years +5 Years * Do you have experience with leading and designing a tour program experience? Yes No * Do you have experience working in a higher education setting? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in university housing or student activities, student conduct, or student affairs area? 0-1 1-2 2-3 years 3+ Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
