    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58506": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator II",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Program Coordinator II Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Program Coordinator II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2027011 Posting/Functional Title Program Coordinator II University Pay Plan Title Program Coordinator II Location San Marcos Department College of Liberal Arts Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $4,002-$4,208.66 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Experience coordinating programs, projects or events. Strong organization skills and meticulous attention to detail. Proven ability to maintain accurate records, files, calendars, and comprehensive project documentation. Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, handle high-pressure deadlines, and adapt to changing program needs. Proficiency with standard office productivity tools. Experience creating clear, professional, and audience-appropriate written materials and visual communications. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing marketing materials, event promotions, flyers, digital signage, newsletters, or other communications materials. Experience managing organizational social media accounts, including LinkedIn, Facebook, and Instagram. Experience updating website content through a content management system. Proficiency with design and content-creation tools, such as Canva or Adobe Creative Cloud. Experience troubleshooting basic presentation technology or coordinating technical support requests. Job Description The Program Coordinator II provides comprehensive program coordination and creative support for the College of Liberal Arts. The position manages the day-to-day operations of select academic programs, supports college-wide events and initiatives, and contributes to communications and promotional projects. Working closely with college leadership, staff, and campus partners, the coordinator helps ensure programs and events are well organized, effectively marketed, and supported. Job Duties Manage day-to-day administrative activities for assigned undergraduate and graduate academic programs and college initiatives. Assist with establishing courses for academic programs and coordinating faculty. Submit purchase requisitions and reimbursements for assigned academic programs. Manage scholarships associated with assigned academic programs. Perform student overrides and assist with other routine academic program-related requests. Communicate regularly with students, faculty, staff, and campus partners regarding academic program activities and administrative needs. Schedule guest speakers and coordinate all aspects of their visits, including vendor registration, payment for services, travel arrangements, and event logistics. Provide in-person administrative coverage for the College of Liberal Arts office during regular business hours as needed. Coordinate and support events for students, faculty, staff and alumni, including reservations, room setup, supplies, signage, attendee communication, and day-of support. Assist with managing assigned webpages and social media channels, including LinkedIn, Facebook, and Instagram. Create marketing materials for programs, special events, and college initiatives. Maintain organized program records, calendars, files, templates, and reference materials. Set up, test, and provide basic support for presentation technology used during meetings, events, and programs. Facilitate special requests from the Dean and Associate Deans. Assist with college-wide projects and other duties as assigned. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 09/16/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58460 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation #1 Curriculum Vitae DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
